      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The way the cops react is always different depending on who they're dealing with. In the immigrant area, the hustlers will try to look like they're just running a legitimate shop, using their language to deflect suspicion, while the cops are wary of getting tangled up in their tight-knit community. In the traditionally Black neighborhood, the tension is immediate and explosive; the community is already on edge, and the police presence is seen not as an investigation, but as an invasion, leading to immediate, volatile confrontations. The difference is between calculated evasion and outright, simmering defiance.",
